                            <comment id="17572256" author="githubbot" created="Thu, 28 Jul 2022 06:39:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reamer commented on PR #4436:&lt;br/&gt;
URL: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4436#issuecomment-1197727478&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4436#issuecomment-1197727478&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;   `tools.jar` should not be used any further. In JDK 9 `tools.jar` and `rt.jar` was even removed from the JDK.&lt;br/&gt;
   We should better raise the dependency that `tools.jar` needs during runtime. Take a look at &lt;a href=&quot;https://openjdk.org/jeps/220&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://openjdk.org/jeps/220&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

</comment>
                            <comment id="17572275" author="githubbot" created="Thu, 28 Jul 2022 07:41:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;vjr commented on PR #4436:&lt;br/&gt;
URL: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4436#issuecomment-1197781754&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4436#issuecomment-1197781754&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;   Agreed , although I propose to have this pr merged as interim fix until Zeppelin itself moves to newer JDK version, is this okay?&lt;/p&gt;

</comment>
